  "title": "Deli Meal Recall: Kroger, Publix and Other Stores Affected Across Three States",
  "summary": "Consumers in several states are being urged to check their refrigerators and freezers after federal food safety officials announced a recall involving thousands of pounds of prepared deli meals. Ukrop’s Homestyle Foods, a Richmond, Virginia-based food producer, has recalled approximately 22,880 pounds of prepared food products because some items may contain small pieces of metal. The recalled foods were sold through several major retailers, including Kroger, Publix, Food Lion and Wegmans. The",
